  "result": "The fix is in place: closing a workspace is now final everywhere. The existing suite (617 tests), typecheck and lint all pass, and the temporary end-to-end check I wrote for the six reports passed before I removed it.\n\nThree behaviours you might not expect:\n\n- **Queued webhook deliveries** for a closed workspace are marked failed (\"the organization has been closed\") rather than left pending, so they are never sent and never re-claimed.\n- **The retention cleanup job** now skips closed workspaces too, following \"background jobs skip it entirely\". The danger-zone page still says the cleanup job removes the data after the retention window; I left that text alone.\n- **A second close from a stale tab** returns a conflict only to someone who could have closed it (the former owner). Anyone else gets the ordinary \"not a member\" refusal.",
